(Stage 1c — constant folding. A predicate on a statically-typed value
 folds at compile time: `n is a number` is statically true (its print
 runs), `n is a text` is statically false (its print is absent), and
 negation `s is not a number` folds true via the UnaryOp(Not) path.
 Acceptance criterion 3.)

a number called n is 5.
a text called s is "hi".
if n is a number, print "n-is-number".
if n is a text, print "n-is-text".
if s is a text, print "s-is-text".
if s is not a number, print "s-not-number".